Hi, Apologies if this is not the appropriate spot to address this but I figured it would be beneficial for people who stumble across this issue as well. First of all some background info: one of our clients uses a rather (out)dated version of Moodle (1.7). Some time ago they reported that dates from questionnaire questions do not (re)appear in the CSV export. At the same time one could easily see (in the results page) and also (somewhat more difficult, lol) in the database that these columns actually had values. After some debugging I found this (or something similar) in the response_date-part of the response_select-function of the locallib.php file (line numbers vary): 
```text
if (preg_match('/\d\d\d\d-\d\d-\d\d/', $val)) {


    $dateparts = split('-', $val);


   $val = gmmktime(0, 0, 0, $dateparts[1], $dateparts[2], $dateparts[0]); // Unix timestamp


    $val = userdate ( $val, $dateformat);


    
$newrow[] = $val;


}
```
 I think the $newrow[] = $val part should be just after this if-statement instead, because if you dump $nam (function response_select_name) and $response (function generate_csv) the structure seems messed up and doesn't follow the same buildup as other responsetypes in those arrays. When I applied the above change to my code (moved $newrow[] = $val; to just after this if-statement) the downloaded CSV shows the dates perfectly fine. I checked the newest branch of this activity module on https://github.com/remotelearner/ and the code still is in the above setup, so I assume this issue is still present. Can anyone refute / acknowledge that: - date_responses (still) show up empty in CSV exports - the above fix will remedy this (hey it worked for me ) Thanks!

