Tony, here is a workaround solution, based on my contribution to this quiz discussion . 1- Modify your current Questionnaire theme, by adding these CSS rules at the end of the theme you are using, e.g. default: 
```text
.addInfo {position: fixed; top: 130px; left: 0px;width:200px;
border: #666666 thin solid;
}
#mod-questionnaire-view .box.generalbox {
width:auto;
margin-left:200px;
margin-right:auto;
}
```
 If you want to have this "pseudo-block" displayed only for certain of your questionnaires, then you might copy the existing default theme to e.g. default_block.css. 2- In your questionnaire, go to the Advanced Settings tab and switch to the modified theme default_block (or keep default if you need the "block" for all your questionnaires). In the Additional Info box, type your "help links". Save. See attached screen shot for result. Please note that, if your questionnaire's questions extend beyond one screen page, the pseudo-block will still be displayed, as it will "follow" the scroll-down. This may not work in all browsers, so needs to be tested before putting on a production server . Tested in FF. Joseph

